## PART C — Closing statement

"To summarize: safety complaints can be turned into structured, traceable defect signals using AI, without letting AI invent the facts. Those signals can be evaluated historically without contaminating the detector with future information. Deterministic risk scoring makes every alert auditable. A single-case success did not generalize — Detector v1 measured 10% target-qualified sensitivity on our validation cohort. And controlled experiments rejected tempting fixes that would not have actually improved discrimination.

Our most important result is not that every recall can already be predicted early. It's that early-defect detection can be investigated with an auditable, leakage-safe, falsifiable framework — and that framework told us the truth, including when the truth was inconvenient."

