## PART E — Master Q&A (big-picture questions not tied to one slide/tab)

- Q: "Is this production-ready?"
  A: "No — it's a validated research prototype. No authentication layer, no database, no scheduler yet. That's explicitly the next phase, not this one."
- Q: "Why does the AI matter at all if the scoring is deterministic?"
  A: "Because the input is free-text written by ordinary people in wildly different words for the same failure. The AI's job is exactly that translation step — normalizing language — which a fixed keyword list cannot do robustly at scale."
- Q: "How is this different from a generic 'AI recall predictor' demo?"
  A: "Almost every flashy version of this either lets the model see future information, or never checks its own results against real history at all. We refuse to do either, which is why our number is 10% instead of a suspiciously perfect 90%."
- Q: "What's next?"
  A: "Grow the validation cohort further, fix the diagnosed matching-and-risk gaps with evidence rather than guesswork, and re-run the exact same locked test to measure the real delta — never declare success without re-testing."